egions of the lands of always  winter they wielded razor thin swords of  ice and raised White's to fight the  living the children of the forest and  their allies the first men fought  valiantly against them but were driven  southwards by their advance the White  Walkers were eventually beat back when  it was discovered that weapons made of  dragonglass could kill them the story  goes that the last hero sought out the  children of the forest who gave him this  information and then the last hero  founded the Nights Watch who were able  to drive the others back in the battle  for the dawn that's pretty much all we  know for sure and it's important to  remember that this is the Westerosi  account of the story which differs from  the legends further ease even though  they're different they basically all  tell the same story if you're a show  only fan you might be thinking well what  the hell didn't the children of the  forest create the White Walkers to which  the answer is yes only that hasn't been  revealed in the books yet so nothing  more is known about it we sort of know  that a guy named bran the Builder who  might or might not have been the last  hero built the wall to stop this sort of  thing from happening in the future  I say sort of no because george RR  martin has made comments to the effect  of we don't really know if bran the  Builder ever lives I went into that in  more detail in my video about the wall  coming down so I'm not going to go over  it again but it all ties back to what I  was talking about just a just a minute  ago what do we really know about why the  White Walkers are returning right now if  anything obviously there are deviations  in how they  are depicted in the show compared to the  source material the way I look at it  major events will be the same but how we  get there will be different so I don't  think Dan and Dave made up the idea that  the children on the forests created  White Walkers as a weapon against men  they just changed the 